{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"recurrent weight sharing across time recurrent weight sharing across time","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md","fileName":"Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 02:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Recurrent Sequence Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Recurrent Sequence Architecture","Recurrent Neural Network","Time-Unrolled Recurrent Network","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"recurrent weight sharing across time recurrent weight sharing across time","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md","fileName":"Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time","heading":"Recurrent Weight Sharing Across Time","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An [[Recurrent Neural Network]] applies the same recurrent connection weights at each step of a sequence. When the network is [[Time-Unrolled Recurrent Network|unrolled]], the arrows between successive hidden states depict repeated uses of one parameter set, not new parameters for each time position.\n\nThis allows a sequence-processing rule to be reused regardless of the step being processed. It also creates a training difficulty: a gradient traveling through many steps repeatedly passes through transformations involving the same